# Everything in this project is committed, including derived data, coverage
# bundles, cached simulation output and the measurement-bearing reports. The
# repository is private and the root README's licence note governs
# redistribution.
#
# What remains excluded is excluded for ONE reason: GitHub rejects any single
# file over 100 MB, so committing these would fail the push rather than store
# them. Each line records the size and how to regenerate it. To track one
# anyway, `git lfs track` the pattern and delete the line.

# 429 MB and 397 MB. USGS 3DEP 1/3 arc-second, public domain, re-downloadable
# from The National Map for bbox 41.9225,-93.8921 -> 42.0492,-93.6588.
# src/propagation.py mosaics them into data/dem10.npz, which IS committed.
terrain-approach/data/USGS_13_*.tif

# 127 MB. Geofabrik extract; scene/clip_osm.py cuts ames.osm from it, and that
# clipped file is committed.
sionna-approach/**/iowa-latest.osm.pbf

# 148 MB, rebuilt by build_terrain_3dep.py.
sionna-approach/**/Terrain3DEP.ply

# 40 MB and 375 MB, rebuilt by import_scene.py / make_blend_3dep.py. The glob
# covers "scene copy/" too, which the old scene/ rules missed because the
# directory name contains a space.
sionna-approach/**/*.blend
sionna-approach/**/*.blend1

# Nothing else is excluded. Compiled bytecode is committed too, on the explicit
# instruction to push everything GitHub will accept -- it is machine-specific and
# regenerated on every run, so expect churn in diffs.

# The one addition to the policy above, on the instruction to "forget scene copy":
# it is a byte-for-byte working copy of scene/ made to hand over the building meshes,
# not a distinct artifact. Its .blend and Terrain3DEP files are already covered above.
sionna-approach/scene copy/
